language: sizes <= 11, 86265 functions on 6x6 inputs

== Part 1: isolation of named functions ==
K = least size. R = distance (number of inputs out of 36) to the nearest other function
of size <= K. 'within r' = least size of another function within distance r ('>11' = none of size <= 11).
function                     K    R  r<=1   r<=2   r<=3   r<=5   r<=6   r<=8   r<=11  r<=17   term
successor  x+1               2   30       7      7      7      5      4      4      4      4  S(x)
addition   x+y               5   24       7      7      7      7      7      7      7      7  It(x,S(a),y)
monus      x-y               5   10       7      7      7      7      7      7      4      1  It(y,P(a),x)
product    x*y               8   16     >11    >11    >11      9      9      9      9      7  It(x,It(y,S(a),a),a)
double     2x                5   24      10     10     10      8      7      7      7      7  It(x,S(a),x)
max(x,y)                     8    6      10     10     10      9      6      5      4      1  ifz(It(x,P(a),y),x,y)
min(x,y)                     8    6      10     10     10      9      6      5      4      1  It(It(x,P(a),y),x,y)
[x = y]                     not expressible with size <= 11
[x <= y]                     9    6      10     10     10     10      9      9      5      2  It(It(y,P(a),x),0,S(a))
|x - y|                     not expressible with size <= 11
x+y+1                        6   24       8      8      8      8      8      8      8      8  S(It(x,S(a),y))
add, but 0 where x=0         8    5      10     10     10      5      5      5      5      5  ifz(x,x,It(x,S(a),y))
add, but y+1 where x=0       7    1       7      7      7      7      5      5      5      5  S(It(y,S(a),P(x)))
add, but 1 at (0,0)          7    1       5      5      5      5      5      5      5      5  S(P(It(x,S(a),y)))
add, but x where y<=1        9    1       9      9      9      9      5      5      5      5  It(x,S(a),It(P(y),y,a))

== Part 2: how many functions are isolated ==
f is isolated at radius r if every other function within distance < r of f has larger size
(delta = r/36). Entries: number isolated / number of functions of that size.
  K   count  r=1      r=2      r=3      r=6      r=9      r=12     r=18    
  1       3         3        3        3        3        3        3        3
  2       5         5        5        5        5        5        5        5
  3       7         7        7        7        7        5        5        5
  4      15        15       15       15        9        7        7        3
  5      70        70       70       70       20       12        8        6
  6     215       215      201      201       58       18       14       12
  7     558       558      503      447      162       40       28       24
  8    1550      1550     1301     1096      394       97       67       48
  9    5359      5359     3905     3196      969      260      166       73
 10   18617     18617    12486     9542     2554      657      384      100
 11   59866     59866    39299    27184     6682     1422      645      112
all   86265     86265    57795    41766    10863     2526     1332      391

== Part 3: surviving dissent after random data ==
Data: n inputs drawn uniformly with replacement, labelled by f. For each input x outside the
data, dissent(x) = least size of a function consistent with the data whose value at x differs
from f(x). Each cell gives three fractions of (trial, x) pairs:
  a = dissent <= K(f)       (f is not yet the strict Occam answer at x)
  b = dissent <= K(f) + 2
  c = dissent <= 11          (some enumerated function still dissents)
and then e = mean posterior probability of a wrong value at x under the prior 8^-K(g)
restricted to the class (functions of size > 11 are left out, so e is a lower estimate).
'vanilla' = all functions; 'patch-free r' = functions isolated at radius r.

